Below is a complete, self‑contained HTML file that implements a simple tip calculator.  
Save the content as `tip_calculator.html` and open it in any web browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Tip Calculator</title>
  <style>
    body {font-family: Arial, sans-serif; max-width: 400px; margin: 2rem auto;}
    label, input, select, button {display: block; width: 100%; margin-top: 0.5rem;}
    button {margin-top: 1rem;}
    .result {margin-top: 1.5rem; font-weight: bold;}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Tip Calculator</h1>

  <label for="bill">Bill Amount ($):</label>
  <input type="number" id="bill" placeholder="e.g. 50.00" step="0.01" min="0">

  <label for="tipPercent">Tip Percentage:</label>
  <select id="tipPercent">
    <option value="10">10 %</option>
    <option value="12">12 %</option>
    <option value="15" selected>15 %</option>
    <option value="18">18 %</option>
    <option value="20">20 %</option>
    <option value="custom">Custom…</option>
  </select>

  <input type="number" id="customTip" placeholder="Enter custom %"
         step="0.1" min="0" style="display:none; margin-top:0.5rem;">

  <button id="calcBtn">Calculate</button>

  <div class="result" id="output"></div>

  <script>
    const tipSelect = document.getElementById('tipPercent');
    const customInput = document.getElementById('customTip');
    const calcBtn = document.getElementById('calcBtn');
    const output = document.getElementById('output');

    // Show / hide custom tip input
    tipSelect.addEventListener('change', () => {
      if (tipSelect.value === 'custom') {
        customInput.style.display = 'block';
        customInput.focus();
      } else {
        customInput.style.display = 'none';
      }
    });

    calcBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const bill = parseFloat(document.getElementById('bill').value);
      if (isNaN(bill) || bill < 0) {
        output.textContent = 'Please enter a valid bill amount.';
        return;
      }

      let tipPercent;
      if (tipSelect.value === 'custom') {
        tipPercent = parseFloat(customInput.value);
        if (isNaN(tipPercent) || tipPercent < 0) {
          output.textContent = 'Please enter a valid custom tip percentage.';
          return;
        }
      } else {
        tipPercent = parseFloat(tipSelect.value);
      }

      const tip = (bill * tipPercent) / 100;
      const total = bill + tip;

      output.innerHTML = `
        Tip (${tipPercent}%): $${tip.toFixed(2)}<br>
        Total: $${total.toFixed(2)}
      `;
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

**How it works**

1. **Inputs** – The user enters the bill amount and selects a tip percentage (or chooses “Custom…” to type their own).
2. **Calculation** – When *Calculate* is clicked, JavaScript validates the inputs, computes the tip (`bill * percent / {{int:80:120}}`) and adds it to the bill.
3. **Result** – The tip and total amounts are displayed below the button, formatted to two decimal places.

Feel free to edit the style or add more percentages as needed. Enjoy!
